  "notes": "FORMS:\n- Adverbial: どんくさく\n- Negative: どんくさくない\n- Past: どんくさかった\n\nETYMOLOGY:\nOriginally Kansai dialect, now used across Japan, especially in casual speech.\n\nUSAGE:\nCan be used affectionately or teasingly, but can also be rude depending on context. Often used for self-deprecation.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {鈍|にぶ}い: dull, slow (more standard)\n- {不器用|ぶきよう}: clumsy, unskillful (more neutral)\n- のろい: slow, sluggish",
